# Fire and Brimstone (windurst 73) while Sin Hunting is accepted (a RNG 60, The Fanged One completed by GM):
# Sin Hunting's 524 is an Event (it outranks his default 338), so the interaction framework alternates it with his
# script. The script's turns: Sin Hunting accepted (not completed): no 531, no 528; var 0: nothing from either quest, so
# the framework plays its 524 after all; var 2 (GM): 532.
char zone=WindurstWoods pos=116.0,-3.7,90.45 job=RNG lvl=60
quest Windurst.SinHunting accepted
quest Windurst.TheFangedOne completed
login
trigger Perih_Vashai                    # the framework's turn: Sin Hunting's 524
finish
trigger Perih_Vashai                    # the script's turn: Sin Hunting accepted, RNG 60, available: no 531: 524
finish
trigger Perih_Vashai                    # the framework's turn: 524
finish
trigger Perih_Vashai                    # the script's turn: var 0: 524
finish
trigger Perih_Vashai                    # the framework's turn: 524
finish
charvar fireAndBrimstone 2
trigger Perih_Vashai                    # the script's turn: var 2: 532
finish
